## 03 — Troubleshooting and Diagnostic Documentation

### Investigation Approach

The simulated investigation focused on determining whether the Outlook connectivity issue was related to network access, email service availability, application configuration, or the local Outlook profile.

### Diagnostic Checklist

| Step | Diagnostic Action | Purpose |
|------|-------------------|---------|
| 1 | Confirm the reported error | Establish the symptoms |
| 2 | Check network connectivity | Identify connectivity issues |
| 3 | Verify access to other resources | Determine the scope of the failure |
| 4 | Review Outlook connection settings | Identify configuration problems |
| 5 | Check Outlook profile health | Investigate local profile issues |
| 6 | Review cached mailbox data | Assess potential synchronization problems |

### Example Work Notes

The following work notes were prepared for the simulated ticket:

```text
User reported that Microsoft Outlook could not connect
to the organization's email server.

Troubleshooting documentation:

1. Confirmed the reported Outlook connectivity error.
2. Checked workstation network connectivity.
3. Verified access to other network resources.
4. Reviewed Outlook connection settings.
5. Investigated potential Outlook profile issues.
6. Considered local mailbox cache corruption as
   a possible contributing factor.

Simulated corrective action:
Recreated the Outlook profile and allowed the
local mailbox cache to rebuild.

Simulated validation:
Outlook successfully connected and mailbox
synchronization was restored.
```

