# 📚 Lessons Learned

### 1. Incident Documentation Is Essential

Accurate incident records provide visibility into reported issues, troubleshooting activities, and resolution history.

### 2. Prioritization Supports Service Delivery

Impact and urgency assessments help support teams determine how incidents should be prioritized according to business needs.

### 3. Assignment Establishes Accountability

Assigning incidents to the appropriate support group and analyst helps establish ownership of the support request.

### 4. Work Notes Preserve Technical Knowledge

Internal work notes provide a record of diagnostic activities and help other analysts understand previous troubleshooting actions.

### 5. Resolution and Closure Serve Different Purposes

Resolution indicates that corrective action has been applied, while closure records the completion of the incident handling process according to the organization's workflow.

### 6. Incident Management and Problem Management Are Related

Recurring incidents may require further investigation through Problem Management to identify underlying causes and prevent future occurrences.

